      "slug": "satin-stitch-angle",
      "term": "Satin stitch angle",
      "definition": "The direction the stitches run across a shape. Choosing the angle before starting determines how the light catches the finished surface."
    }
  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Flat satin stitch runs parallel stitches at a chosen ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "satin stitch angle",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "satin-stitch-angle"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": " from one edge of the shape to the other. Each stitch lies exactly alongside the previous one with no gaps and no overlaps. The angle is decided before starting and kept constant throughout the shape.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton, 3 to 4 strands; or silk thread for maximum lustre"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fabric",
              "value": "Closely woven linen or cotton"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needle",
              "value": "Embroidery needle size 7 or 8"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hoop",
              "value": "15 cm or 20 cm embroidery hoop"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Working a practice piece",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Transfer the shape outline onto the fabric. Decide the stitch angle (usually 45 degrees to the grain).",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring the needle up at one edge of the shape and insert at the opposite edge. Pull through smoothly.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring up immediately alongside the first stitch and repeat, filling the shape from one side to the other.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Keep each stitch at the same angle and pack them tightly so no fabric shows through.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Common mistakes",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "intro": "Two common problems.",
          "items": [
            {
              "fix": "Lay each stitch at exactly the same angle. Pull each through with consistent gentle tension.",
              "cause": "Stitches are not lying parallel or tension varies between them.",
              "symptom": "The surface looks ridged or uneven"
            },
            {
              "fix": "Work split stitch or back stitch around the outline first. Satin stitches taken to the edge of this padding line give a crisp border.",
              "cause": "The stitches are not meeting the outline exactly.",
              "symptom": "The shape edge is ragged"
            }
          ],
          "heading": "When flat satin stitch goes wrong"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Uses and related stitches"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Satin stitch is the base for "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "padded satin stitch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "embroidery-padded-satin-stitch",
                  "label": "padded satin stitch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which raises the surface over a foundation, and for the shaded fills of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "encroaching satin stitch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "embroidery-encroaching-satin-stitch",
                  "label": "encroaching satin stitch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "long and short stitch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "embroidery-long-and-short-stitch",
                  "label": "long and short stitch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". A worked outline of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "split stitch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "embroidery-split-stitch",
                  "label": "split stitch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " under the edge gives the crisp border satin needs to fill petals, leaves, and geometric shapes cleanly."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
